      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Preserve settings window position",
        "body": "Fixes #17\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nPreserve the Settings window position across app launches.\r\n\r\nThe Settings window is created manually with AppKit and was previously centered every time it was recreated. That meant users lost their preferred Settings window placement after quitting and relaunching Nameplate.\r\n\r\nThis change gives the Settings window a stable AppKit frame autosave name and restores any saved frame before falling back to centering. The window is only centered when no saved frame exists, so a restored frame is not overwritten.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- `git diff --check`\r\n- `swift build`\r\n\r\nSource proof:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPROOF autosave-name-defined=true\r\nPROOF restore-before-autosave=true\r\nPROOF center-guarded-after-restore=true\r\n```",
        "branch": "fix/issue-17-settings-window-autosave",
